; An ordinary beancount file: valid beancount, and not one this tool wrote.
;
; Its transaction carries none of the `gnucash-*` metadata an export adds, and
; the parser refuses it on the first of those it looks for — which is the check
; that makes "only beancount files exported from GnuCash can be imported" true.
;
; The account declaration *is* fully annotated, so the refusal has to come from
; the transaction rather than from the first line of the file: a parser that
; gave up earlier would refuse this for the wrong reason and pass a test that
; only asked whether it refused.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_cli_beancount.py.
2024-01-01 open Assets:Bank CAD
  gnucash-name: "Assets:Bank"
  gnucash-guid: "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
  gnucash-type: "BANK"
  gnucash-placeholder: "false"

2024-01-15 * "Payee" "Groceries"
  Assets:Bank  -50.00 CAD
  Expenses:Food  50.00 CAD
